Steps: `<ol><li>Warm up</li><li>Run</li><li>Cool down</li></ol>` — the `ol` gives the items order semantics and numbers them. Standings: `<table><thead><tr><th>Place</th><th>Runner</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Amara</td><td>12:04</td></tr></tbody></table>` — the table lets a screen reader read each cell against its column header. Code: `<pre><code>function add(a, b) {
  return a + b;
}</code></pre>` — `pre` preserves the whitespace so the indentation and line breaks survive, and `code` marks the text as code. Each fix replaces a presentational `<div>` with the element that actually carries the meaning.

